  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the management of peatlands and the capacities of stakeholders in Indonesia (Peat-IMPACTS Indonesia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">50 per cent of Indonesia&apos;s peatlands have been converted and degraded by excessive land use and fire. The project aims at sustainable and climate-friendly management of peatlands at the landscape level. The approach focussed on building technical and institutional resources and skills in peatland restoration, involving the private sector in areas such as paludiculture and the impact of fire on peatlands.  Through the project work, local livelihoods were preserved. The exchange of lessons learnt ensured dissemination at national level. Emission reductions achieved have contributed to the achievement of the Indonesian NDC and the 2015-2020 development plan.</narrative>
  </description>
